{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He it was the shalit, etc.</b> That is, even though he was the shalit (viceroy), and it is not the way of a ruler to involve himself with the selling of grain — and all the more so with so vast a wondrous burden — nonetheless he himself was the one who provided rations for all the people of the land, and his hidden motive was with him, to recognize [them] when his brothers came down."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:54.054651913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}